{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"Module 10 — Data Security\nStates → Access → At-rest Encrypt → Secure Comm → Masking → Backup → Retain → Destroy → DLP → Integrity","x":-560,"y":-2720,"width":460,"height":60,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b1","type":"text","text":"Importance + 3 states (LO01)\nCritical data via business impact analysis\nData secured = prevent destruction/modification/\ndisclosure + recover + retention/destruction policies\nData at Rest (inactive, stored) → encryption,\npassword protection, tokenization, access control\nData in Use (RAM/processing) → authentication,\nfull memory encryption, strong identity, patching\nData in Transit (moving) → SSL/TLS, PGP/S-MIME,\nfirewall, DLP","x":-1650,"y":-2500,"width":380,"height":260,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"b2","type":"text","text":"Access Controls (LO02)\nModels: RBAC · Rule-based (RB-RBAC) · MAC · DAC\nImplement logically: ACLs · Group Policy · account\nrestrictions · passwords/access tokens\nWindows ACL: access token vs ACEs; 6 ACE types\n(3 generic + 3 object-specific); share vs NTFS perms\nLinux ACL: setfacl -m u:user:perm · -x · -b ·\nsetfacl -m d:o:rx /Testdir · getfacl (mask rule)\nAccount restrictions: logon hours + expiration;\npam_time /etc/security/time.conf","x":-1650,"y":-2160,"width":380,"height":270,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"b3","type":"text","text":"At-Rest Encryption (LO03)\n4 categories: disk · file-level · removable · database\nWindows: Device Encryption (TPM+UEFI) · BitLocker\n(AES-CBC/XTS 128/256) · TPM 2.0 (Windows 11)\nEFS (cipher /e · /w:dir) · third-party file tools\nmacOS FileVault 2 · Linux dm-crypt Plain vs LUKS\nAndroid dm-crypt AES-128-CBC (4 states) · iOS default\nDatabase: SQL Server TDE (DEK→cert→master key,\nALTER DATABASE SET ENCRYPTION ON) · Always\nEncrypted (randomized vs deterministic, client-side\nkeys) · Oracle TDE (columns/tablespace + wallet)","x":-1650,"y":-1810,"width":380,"height":330,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"b4","type":"text","text":"Secure Communication (LO04)\nBrowser↔Web: 6-step TLS handshake; standard vs EV\nSSL; certificate Details (Issued To/By, SHA-256\nfingerprints)\nIIS: Create Certificate Request (CSR, DN fields,\nMicrosoft RSA SChannel CSP) → complete → bind\nhttps/443\nDB↔Web: SQL Server Force Encryption (Configuration\nManager Flags); Oracle Advanced Security SSL (wallet)\nEmail: Outlook S/MIME (Trust Center → Email\nSecurity; sign/encrypt certs + algorithms); O365\nMessage Encryption (IRM, E3); Gmail S/MIME","x":-1150,"y":-2500,"width":430,"height":310,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b5","type":"text","text":"Data Masking (LO05)\nObfuscation: preserve format, change keys\n(2424 XXXX XXXX 3421)\nTypes: SDM (at rest) · DDM (in transit, proxy-altered\nSQL) · on-the-fly (environment-to-environment)\nAlgorithms: scrambling · lookup substitution ·\nnulling · shuffling · number/date variance ·\nmasking out · date aging · pseudonymization · averaging\nTechniques: substitution · tokenization · FPE ·\nhashing · data shifting\nSQL Server DDM (default(), email()) · Oracle data\nmasking F.A.S.T. = Find → Access → Secure → Test","x":-1150,"y":-2110,"width":430,"height":330,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b6","type":"text","text":"Backup + Retention (LO06)\n2 purposes: reinstate system · recover after loss\n8-step strategy: data→media→tech→RAID→method→\ntypes→solution→recovery drill\nMedia factors: cost, reliability, speed, availability, usability\nRAID 0/1/3/5/10/50 (50 = stripe-of-mirrors, min 6)\nSAN (block) vs NAS (file: CIFS/SMB+NFS)\nFull/Incremental/Differential · File History (10 min–\ndaily) · Time Machine (hourly/daily/weekly)\nOracle cold vs hot (RMAN+ARCHIVELOG) · cPanel\nfull backup · retention policy (HIPAA/SOX/IRS/\nCOPPA/GDPR; team; per-type periods)","x":-1150,"y":-1700,"width":430,"height":350,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"b7","type":"text","text":"Data Destruction (LO07)\nPurpose: restrict unauthorized disclosure (delete ≠ gone)\nTechniques: Clearing (overwrite/wiping/erasure vs\nkeyboard) · Purging (degauss / Secure Erase vs\nlaboratory) · Destroying (disintegrate/incinerate/\nshred ≤2mm) · Disposal (non-confidential)\nDiskPart wipe: list disk → select disk 1 → clean →\ncreate partition primary → active → format NTFS\nTools: DBAN (free OSS, HDD-only, no SSD, no audit\ncert) · Macrorit · KillDisk (DoD 5220.22-M)\nStandards: NIST SP 800-88 Clear/Purge/Destroy ·\nDoD 5220.22-M 3-pass (0→1→random) · PCI Req 9.10\n· HIPAA · ISO/IEC 27001\n6 best practices incl. e-waste recycling","x":650,"y":-2500,"width":430,"height":380,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"b8","type":"text","text":"DLP (LO08)\nSoftware + processes blocking confidential data\nleaving the org (data leak / information loss /\nextrusion prevention)\nEndpoint DLP → data in use (clipboard, USB, print)\nNetwork DLP → data in transit (perimeter; SSL, IM)\nStorage DLP → data at rest (file servers, SharePoint, DB)\nWindows Information Protection + Azure Information\nProtection · MyDLP (open source) · Safend DPS,\nSymantec, McAfee, Trustwave, Digital Guardian","x":650,"y":-2040,"width":430,"height":260,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"b9","type":"text","text":"Data Integrity (LO09)\nAccuracy + consistency + reliability throughout lifecycle\n(GDPR-enabled)\nCharacteristics: Complete · Accurate · Safe ·\nCompliance · Consistent · Reliable · Timeliness\nTypes: Physical (storage; error-correcting memory,\nbattery-protected write cache, RAID) + Logical\n(4 subtypes: entity · referential · domain ·\nuser-defined)\nChecking: checksums/hashes (MD5, SHA-256, SHA-3) ·\nparity · CRC · validation rules · ECC · signatures\nChecklist: validate input/data · remove duplicates ·\nbackups · least-privilege access · audit trail","x":650,"y":-1700,"width":430,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"end","type":"text","text":"Lifecycle flow\nCreate → Store (rest) → Access (control) → Use\n(memory) → Transit (SSL/TLS) → Mask (optional) →\nBackup (RAID/SAN-NAS) → Retain (policy) → Destroy\n(Clear/Purge/Destroy) → Protect throughout (DLP + \nintegrity checks + audit trail)\nEncryption at rest + in transit + masking + DLP +\ndestruction = defense in depth for data security\nOnly material in the PDFs; no invented facts","x":1150,"y":-2190,"width":430,"height":230,"color":"5"}
	],
